            <ArticleTitle>A Rare Case of Gastrointestinal Tract Foreign Body; Glassy Stomach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e44</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ingestion of foreign bodies is common and conservative treatment can eliminated most particlesfrom the gastrointestinal tractunless peritoneal signs appear. A 22-year-old man presented to emergency department who had ingested glass particles of a crushed beveragebottle.Hecomplained ofepigastric and periumbilical pain. Physical examination did not revealany peritoneal signs. Abdominal X-ray showed stomach full of small glass particles. Conservative treatment, without any surgical intervention,resulted insafely eliminating glass particlesin this patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
